  'typhoon-haiyan-2013', 'Haiyan', 'Typhoon Haiyan',
  2013, '2013 Pacific', 'WP',
  5, 'Typhoon',
  NULL, NULL,
  '2013-06-01',
  NULL, NULL,
  ARRAY[]::TEXT[],
  'Typhoon Haiyan, known in the Philippines as Super Typhoon Yolanda, was an extremely powerful and catastrophic tropical cyclone that is among the most intense tropical cyclones ever recorded. Upon making landfall, Haiyan devastated portions of Southeast Asia, particularly the Philippines, during early November 2013. It is one of the deadliest typhoons on record in the Philippines, killing at least 6,300 people in the region of Visayas alone. It was the most intense and deadliest tropical cyclone ',
  '## Overview

Typhoon Haiyan, known in the Philippines as Super Typhoon Yolanda, was an extremely powerful and catastrophic tropical cyclone that is among the most intense tropical cyclones ever recorded. Upon making landfall, Haiyan devastated portions of Southeast Asia, particularly the Philippines, during early November 2013. It is one of the deadliest typhoons on record in the Philippines, killing at least 6,300 people in the region of Visayas alone. It was the most intense and deadliest tropical cyclone worldwide in 2013.

## Key Facts

See structured data above.

## Sources

- [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Typhoon_Haiyan)
- [NOAA NHC](https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/)
',
  ARRAY['Typhoon Haiyan reached Category 5 intensity, the highest on the Saffir-Simpson scale.', 'As a Western Pacific typhoon, Haiyan was named by the Japan Meteorological Agency.'],
